                            <strong>Planning Poker</strong>, also known as <em>Scrum Poker</em>,
                            is a consensus-based estimation technique used by agile teams to
                            assign <strong>story points</strong> to user stories. Each team
                            member privately picks a card representing their estimate, and
                            all cards are revealed simultaneously. This avoids
                            <em>anchoring bias</em> and surfaces real disagreements that lead
                            to better conversations and more accurate sprint forecasts.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            This <strong>free Planning Poker</strong> app is built for modern,
                            distributed agile teams. It uses WebSockets for real-time voting,
                            runs entirely in your browser, requires no account, and is 100%
                            free and open source — making it one of the simplest free Planning
                            Poker tools available online.
                        </p>
